A. Stash commands
Stash temporarily stores unfinished changes so you can switch tasks.
Command	Application
git stash	Temporarily save changes
git stash push -m "message"	Save with description
git stash list	View saved stashes
git stash apply	Restore latest stash but keep it
git stash pop	Restore and remove latest stash
git stash drop	Delete a stash


Tag commands
Tags mark important versions of your project.
Command	Application
git tag	List tags
git tag v1.0	Create lightweight tag
git tag -a v1.0 -m "Release 1.0"	Create annotated tag
git show v1.0	View tag details
git push origin v1.0	Push a specific tag
git push origin --tags	Push all tags
git tag -d v1.0	Delete local tag

Useful advanced commands
Command	Application
git blame file.py	Identify who changed each line
git shortlog -sn	Show commit counts by author
git reflog	View recent HEAD and branch movements
git cherry-pick commit-id	Apply a particular commit
git bisect start	Start searching for a problematic commit
git archive	Create an archive of repository files
git grep "keyword"	Search tracked files


